From 3ae189fb8f3cb40e191b6e77df1aec4a8a884934 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jacob Root <me@rooty.dev>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 01:44:55 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/6] vhost_user_frontend: check every backend mapping against
 its region

A vhost-user backend is another process, and may be a compromised one.
Until now the frontend passed its SHMEM_MAP, GPU_MAP and EXTERNAL_MAP
requests to the shared memory mapper with no check of its own: the
mapper's arena refused a range past the BAR, but nothing refused one past
the region the backend itself reported (the BAR is that length rounded up
to a power of two), a mapping that overlaps a live one (the later MAP_FIXED
silently replaces the earlier one's pages, and unmapping either then tears
down the other's), or an unmap of a range that was never mapped.

Keep the backend's live mappings in the handler and refuse, before
anything is placed:
- a mapping at an offset or file offset that is not page aligned, of
  length zero, or whose pages reach past the region's length;
- a mapping that overlaps a live one (EEXIST);
- an unmap that does not name exactly a live mapping, offset and length.

A length that is not a whole number of pages is taken as the pages it
covers, as mmap takes it.

Also:
- unmap everything the backend mapped on device reset, which the
  vhost-user spec asks of the front-end and was a TODO here;
- a refused request no longer stops the worker (and with it the VM): the
  refusal has already gone back to the backend as the reply, and the
  channel is still in step.

